" x=\"1501\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E17-MJMATHI-61\" x=\"1891\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E17-MJMAIN-2C\" x=\"2420\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E17-MJMATHI-62\" x=\"2865\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E17-MJMAIN-29\" x=\"3295\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> is the greatest common divisor of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.23ex\" height=\"1.676ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -576.1 529.5 721.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-18-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-18-Title\">a</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E18-MJMATHI-61\" d=\"M33 157Q33 258 109 349T280 441Q331 441 370 392Q386 422 416 422Q429 422 439 414T449 394Q449 381 412 234T374 68Q374 43 381 35T402 26Q411 27 422 35Q443 55 463 131Q469 151 473 152Q475 153 483 153H487Q506 153 506 144Q506 138 501 117T481 63T449 13Q436 0 417 -8Q409 -10 393 -10Q359 -10 336 5T306 36L300 51Q299 52 296 50Q294 48 292 46Q233 -10 172 -10Q117 -10 75 30T33 157ZM351 328Q351 334 346 350T323 385T277 405Q242 405 210 374T160 293Q131 214 119 129Q119 126 119 118T118 106Q118 61 136 44T179 26Q217 26 254 59T298 110Q300 114 325 217T351 328Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E18-MJMATHI-61\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> and <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.644ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 708 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-19-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-19-Title\">b.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E19-MJMATHI-62\" d=\"M73 647Q73 657 77 670T89 683Q90 683 161 688T234 694Q246 694 246 685T212 542Q204 508 195 472T180 418L176 399Q176 396 182 402Q231 442 283 442Q345 442 383 396T422 280Q422 169 343 79T173 -11Q123 -11 82 27T40 150V159Q40 180 48 217T97 414Q147 611 147 623T109 637Q104 637 101 637H96Q86 637 83 637T76 640T73 647ZM336 325V331Q336 405 275 405Q258 405 240 397T207 376T181 352T163 330L157 322L136 236Q114 150 114 114Q114 66 138 42Q154 26 178 26Q211 26 245 58Q270 81 285 114T318 219Q336 291 336 325Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E19-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E19-MJMATHI-62\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E19-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"429\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's prove this statement.</p>\n<!--\nRecall that **Bézout’s identity** states that for any two integers [math]a[/math] and [math]b,[/math] there exist integers [math]u[/math] and [math]v[/math] such that \n\\[\nau+bv= \\textrm{gcd}(a,b)\n\\]\nwhere [math] \\textrm{gcd}(a,b)[/math] is the greatest common divisor of [math]a[/math] and [math]b.[/math]\n\nWe'll use Bézout’s identity to prove our next property. \n-->\n<p><strong>Proof</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>Given that <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"13.475ex\" height=\"2.843ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.838ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -863.1 5801.7 1223.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-20-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-20-Title\">\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1,</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E20-MJMAIN-67\" d=\"M329 409Q373 453 429 453Q459 453 472 434T485 396Q485 382 476 371T449 360Q416 360 412 390Q410 404 415 411Q415 412 416 414V415Q388 412 363 393Q355 388 355 386Q355 385 359 381T368 369T379 351T388 